        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-20T17:31:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a way for bcic developers to program a config into CBI without booting the OS: 1. Add a config to the FW; 2. Flash it to a DUT; 3. Run \u0027bcfg set x\u0027. It\u0027s not useful for testing a new battery because flashing FW with a new config is enough. \n\n\u003e Is there a console command to modify the effective battery config? or plan to add one?\n\nIt would be nice to have such a command but it won\u0027t be a small command (unless we sacrifice the ux). Also, it will not be very needed because we\u0027ll eventually be able to program a config from the OS.",
      "parentUuid": "2a4e7058_394d258d",
